WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:05.567
 <i>( harmonica wails )</i>

2
00:00:05.567 --> 00:00:08.901
 <i>( theme music playing )</i>

3
00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:45.467
( laughs )

4
00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.100
OKAY. WE BET $50.000.

5
00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.100
- Roseanne: I CALL.
- IT'S NOT YOUR TURN. MOM.

6
00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.033
I KNOW.
BUT IT'S MY HOUSE.

7
00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:01.033
WE GONNA PLAY POKER.
OR SHOOT THE BREEZE?

8
00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:02.968
- SHOOT THE BREEZE.
- Dan: <i>OKAY.</i>

9
00:01:02.968 --> 00:01:05.701
THE PORTCHESTER GAME.
LAST GAME OF MY SENIOR YEAR.

10
00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:08.367
- ( kids whining )
- WE'RE DOWN BY A TOUCHDOWN
 WITH ONE MINUTE TO GO.

11
00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:11.100
- LET'S PLAY POKER.
- NOW WE GOTTA SHOOT THE BREEZE.
 I GET TO TELL THIS STORY.

12
00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:14.400
- DAD. WE KNOW THIS STORY.
- THIS TIME I'M TELLING IT FROM
 THE REFEREE'S POINT OF VIEW.

13
00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.801
- I GOT A PAIR.
- SO DO I.

14
00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:18.834
YEAH. BUT ROSEANNE'S
ARE SHOWING.

15
00:01:20.234 --> 00:01:23.067
YOU GUYS THINK WE DON'T GET
YOUR CORNY LITTLE SEX JOKES.

16
00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:26.100
HEY. YOU KIDS ARE
OUR CORNY LITTLE SEX JOKES.

17
00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:31.400
 <i>( doorbell rings )</i>

18
00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.667
GEEZ. IT'S THE FUZZ!
HIDE THE CARDS AND THE JIF!

19
00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:37.133
DARLENE. I THINK
IT'S HIGH TIME

20
00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:39.467
WE TAUGHT D.J. HOW TO
PLAY 52-CARD PICKUP.

21
00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:41.601
( laughing )

22
00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.200
( gasps )

23
00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.033
TA-DA!
( laughs )

24
00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:48.033
DAD. WHAT ARE
YOU DOING HERE?

25
00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:50.133
I CAME TO SEE MY
SWEET LITTLE KAPUSHKA.

26
00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:52.801
- AL!
- HEY. DADDY!

27
00:01:52.801 --> 00:01:56.267
DAD!
OH. MY GOSH!

28
00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:58.300
- IS EVERYTHING OKAY?
- FINE. FINE.

29
00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.234
WHERE'S GRANDMA?

30
00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.901
- HERE SHE IS NOW.
- HELLO!

31
00:02:03.901 --> 00:02:05.968
MOM!

32
00:02:05.968 --> 00:02:09.334
- MOM. HI.
- AWW.

33
00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:11.834
WHAT ARE YOU GUYS
DOING IN LANFORD?

34
00:02:11.834 --> 00:02:14.968
WELL. WE GOT UP THIS MORNING
AND I SAID TO YOUR MOTHER.
"WHAT DO YOU WANNA DO?"

35
00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:18.133
AND AS USUAL SHE HAD
NO OPINION. SO I SAID.
"LET'S GO FOR A LITTLE RIDE."

36
00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:21.968
TWO HUNDRED AND FIFTY MILES
ISN'T A LITTLE DRIVE.

37
00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:24.300
ESPECIALLY WHEN YOU HAVE
A WOMAN SITTING NEXT TO YOU

38
00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:27.501
WHO WHENEVER YOU PASS
A CAR SAYS. "I WONDER
WHERE THEY'RE GOING."

39
00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:30.000
BOY. SHE'S GOT PROBLEMS.

40
00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.133
MA. WHY DIDN'T
YOU CALL?

41
00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:35.334
I DID. BUT YOUR
LINE WAS BUSY.

42
00:02:35.334 --> 00:02:37.801
THEN I TRIED YOUR SISTER.
I COULDN'T GET A HOLD OF HER.

43
00:02:37.801 --> 00:02:39.968
I THOUGHT MAYBE SOMETHING
WAS WRONG. BUT OF COURSE.

44
00:02:39.968 --> 00:02:42.467
IF THERE WERE. GOD KNOWS.
SHE WOULD NEVER TELL ME.

45
00:02:42.467 --> 00:02:45.167
MY APARTMENT WAS GETTING
FUMIGATED. MOM. SO--

46
00:02:45.167 --> 00:02:46.934
FUMIGATED FOR WHAT?

47
00:02:46.934 --> 00:02:49.367
ALL THOSE LOUSES
YOU GO OUT WITH?

48
00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:58.734
LET ME SEE IF I
GOT THIS STRAIGHT.

49
00:02:58.734 --> 00:02:59.834
- WE NEED MILK--
- MILK.

50
00:02:59.834 --> 00:03:01.133
- WE NEED EGGS.
- EGGS.

51
00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:02.734
BULLETS.

52
00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:08.067
COME ON. DAN. LET'S JUST
TRY TO GET THROUGH THIS.

53
00:03:08.067 --> 00:03:09.567
( sighs )

54
00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:11.567
Roseanne:
 <i>WHAT ARE YOU DOING UP?</i>

55
00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:13.067
I CAN'T SLEEP.

56
00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:15.467
GRANDPA'S IN THE BATHROOM
MAKING THOSE GAGGING NOISES.

57
00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:17.467
EW.

58
00:03:17.467 --> 00:03:19.300
HOW LONG'S
HE BEEN IN THERE?

59
00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.300
AT LEAST
A HALF AN HOUR.

60
00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.734
WELL. HE'S PROBABLY
GOT IT ALL UP BY NOW.

61
00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:27.133
WHY DON'T YOU
GO BACK TO BED.

62
00:03:27.133 --> 00:03:29.267
MOM. HE'S REALLY
DRIVING ME CRAZY.

63
00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:32.834
IF HE SAYS "PULL MY FINGER"
ONE MORE TIME--

64
00:03:34.601 --> 00:03:38.567
WELL. NOW YOU KNOW
WHERE I GET MY SMART.
SOPHISTICATED WIT.

65
00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:42.334
I CAN'T BELIEVE
THAT MAN RAISED YOU.

66
00:03:42.334 --> 00:03:45.200
NOW YOU KNOW WHY
I WAS SO CRAZY TO
MARRY YOU SO YOUNG.

67
00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.200
I THOUGHT IT WAS BECAUSE
YOU WERE MADLY IN LOVE.

68
00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.968
YEAH. WITH THE IDEA OF
GETTING OUT OF MY HOUSE.

69
00:03:52.801 --> 00:03:55.667
IS THERE A PLACE
IN HERE TO SIT DOWN?

70
00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:59.200
YEAH. WHY DON'T YOU TRY
ONE OF THESE THINGS
WE CALL "CHAIRS"?

71
00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.133
WE SIT IN 'EM
FREQUENTLY.

72
00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:06.033
WHAT KIND OF LIST IS HE MAKING?
NOT THAT IT'S ANY
OF MY BUSINESS.

73
00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:07.467
A HIT LIST.

74
00:04:10.567 --> 00:04:13.267
HE'S JUST GONNA GO
OUT TO THE STORE AND
PICK UP A FEW THINGS.

75
00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:15.834
PLEASE DON'T GET
ANYTHING SPECIAL FOR ME.

76
00:04:15.834 --> 00:04:18.133
I'LL EAT WHATEVER YOU HAVE.
BUT YOUR FATHER'S DIET

77
00:04:18.133 --> 00:04:21.534
IS LOW SODIUM. LOW FAT.
AND HIGH FIBER.

78
00:04:21.534 --> 00:04:23.734
SO WHY DON'T WE JUST GET
HIM SOME WOOD. YOU KNOW?

79
00:04:23.734 --> 00:04:27.367
AND THEN HE CAN PUT MUSTARD
ON IT AND. YOU KNOW.
THAT'D BE A GOOD TREAT.

80
00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:30.701
MUSTARD'S HIGH IN FAT.
A LOT OF PEOPLE DON'T KNOW THAT.

81
00:04:30.701 --> 00:04:33.234
A LOT OF PEOPLE
DON'T CARE.

82
00:04:33.234 --> 00:04:35.767
I DO. BUT DOGGONE IT.
I GOTTA GO.

83
00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:42.133
 <i>( door closes )</i>

84
00:04:42.133 --> 00:04:44.667
- HE'S NOT WORKING. IS HE?
- HE'S WORKING.

85
00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:47.367
WELL. I'M GLAD.
BECAUSE YOUR FATHER WORRIES.

86
00:04:47.367 --> 00:04:49.200
ESPECIALLY ABOUT
YOUR SISTER.

87
00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.534
( sighs )

88
00:04:51.534 --> 00:04:53.534
HE DOESN'T
HAVE TO WORRY.

89
00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:57.167
WELL. SOMEBODY HAS TO.
SHE'S 32. SHE'S UNMARRIED.

90
00:04:57.167 --> 00:04:59.934
HEAVEN FORBID THAT SHE TURNS OUT
TO BE LIKE YOUR AUNT DALE.

91
00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:02.501
WHO TEACHES P.E.

92
00:05:02.501 --> 00:05:06.067
SPEAKING OF AUNT DALE.
HOW IS UNCLE SHIRLEY?

93
00:05:09.634 --> 00:05:12.100
ALSO. YOUR FATHER
IS CONCERNED

94
00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.167
BECAUSE YOUR SISTER
LIVES IN A BUILDING

95
00:05:14.167 --> 00:05:16.267
THAT NEEDS
TO BE FUMIGATED.

96
00:05:16.267 --> 00:05:18.300
BUT I AM HER MOTHER.

97
00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:21.200
IT IS NOT MY JOB
TO TELL HER WHAT TO DO.

98
00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.701
OH. I GET IT.

99
00:05:22.701 --> 00:05:26.267
BUT IT IS YOUR JOB TO TELL ME
TO TELL HER WHAT TO DO.

100
00:05:26.267 --> 00:05:29.601
YES. I'M SURE PETUNIAS
ARE PERENNIALS.

101
00:05:35.167 --> 00:05:38.067
JACKIE. MOM WAS JUST
TALKING ABOUT YOU.

102
00:05:38.067 --> 00:05:40.901
NOW YOU GET TO LISTEN
WHILE SHE TALKS ABOUT ME.

103
00:05:44.834 --> 00:05:46.968
SO. ARE WE GONNA
TALK ABOUT ROSEANNE?

104
00:05:46.968 --> 00:05:50.300
CERTAINLY NOT.
IT'S JUST THAT YOUR FATHER
IS WORRIED ABOUT HER.

105
00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:52.667
SHE SEEMS SO TIRED
ALL THE TIME.

106
00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:54.200
MAMA...

107
00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:57.267
YOU'VE BEEN HERE
A GRAND TOTAL OF ONE HOUR.

108
00:05:57.267 --> 00:05:59.467
HOW DO YOU KNOW
HOW TIRED SHE IS?

109
00:05:59.467 --> 00:06:02.434
A MOTHER KNOWS.

110
00:06:02.434 --> 00:06:04.934
GRANTED. IT IS
A DIFFERENT GENERATION.

111
00:06:04.934 --> 00:06:08.367
BUT YOUR FATHER
WOULD HAVE DIED BEFORE
HE MADE ME GO OUT TO WORK.

112
00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:10.767
DAN DOESN'T MAKE
ROSEANNE WORK.

113
00:06:10.767 --> 00:06:12.834
THAT'S WHAT
SHE TELLS YOU.

114
00:06:12.834 --> 00:06:15.901
BUT YOU'VE NEVER BEEN MARRIED.
YOU DON'T KNOW THESE THINGS.

115
00:06:17.033 --> 00:06:19.033
WHAT'D YOU FIND OUT
ABOUT ME?

116
00:06:19.033 --> 00:06:21.367
YOU'RE
VERY TIRED.

117
00:06:21.367 --> 00:06:23.367
HEY. MA. IS TWO
BLANKETS ENOUGH?

118
00:06:23.367 --> 00:06:27.334
TWO'S FINE.
IF THAT'S ALL YOU HAVE.

119
00:06:27.334 --> 00:06:30.200
NO. I HAVE MORE.
HOW MANY WOULD YOU LIKE?

120
00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.567
WHAT DID
YOUR FATHER SAY?

121
00:06:31.567 --> 00:06:35.133
HE SAYS HE'S GONNA BE SLEEPING
OUT IN THE DRIVEWAY NAKED.

122
00:06:36.934 --> 00:06:38.934
HOW MANY BLANKETS
DO YOU WANT. MA?

123
00:06:38.934 --> 00:06:42.000
IF YOU HAVE TWO.
TWO'S FINE.

124
00:06:48.901 --> 00:06:50.901
I AM THIS CLOSE
TO THE EDGE.

125
00:06:50.901 --> 00:06:52.968
AND IF I GO OVER.
I'M TAKING YOU WITH ME.

126
00:06:52.968 --> 00:06:56.367
SHE DOES HAVE A WAY
ABOUT HER. DOESN'T SHE?

127
00:06:56.367 --> 00:06:59.434
IF SHE WANTS TO RAG ON
YOUR LIFE. WHY DOESN'T
SHE JUST TELL YOU?

128
00:06:59.434 --> 00:07:02.300
I'M GETTING SO SICK OF
THESE BEHIND-THE-BACK
CONVERSATIONS.

129
00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:04.901
YOU MEAN. LIKE THE ONE
WE'RE HAVING ABOUT
MOM RIGHT NOW?

130
00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.067
- YEAH.
- YEAH.

131
00:07:08.067 --> 00:07:11.734
I MEAN. WHY SHOULD
I HAVE TO DEFEND THE
GUYS YOU GO OUT WITH?

132
00:07:11.734 --> 00:07:13.501
YOU SHOULDN'T.

133
00:07:13.501 --> 00:07:15.501
AND I'M TIRED OF
EXPLAINING TO HER

134
00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:18.267
WHY YOUR HOUSE IS
SO FILTHY ALL THE TIME.

135
00:07:20.601 --> 00:07:22.434
YEAH. THAT'S
MY BUSINESS.

136
00:07:22.434 --> 00:07:24.434
YEAH. SHE JUST
DOESN'T LET UP.

137
00:07:24.434 --> 00:07:26.701
WELL. SHE'S GONNA LET UP.
BECAUSE I'M GONNA LAY INTO HER.

138
00:07:26.701 --> 00:07:28.434
WELL. I'M GONNA
LAY INTO HER TOO.

139
00:07:28.434 --> 00:07:30.634
THAT WOMAN'S NOT QUALIFIED
TO JUDGE ANYBODY'S LIFE.

140
00:07:30.634 --> 00:07:32.167
- WHERE IS SHE?
- MOM?!

141
00:07:32.167 --> 00:07:34.300
ENOUGH IS ENOUGH ALREADY.
WE GOTTA DO THIS.

142
00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:35.467
ABSOLUTELY.

143
00:07:35.467 --> 00:07:38.467
I FOUND THIS UNDER
YOUR SISTER'S SOFA.

144
00:07:39.634 --> 00:07:41.467
MOM. WHY ARE YOU
GIVING IT TO ME?

145
00:07:41.467 --> 00:07:44.167
IT'S HER POTATO CHIPS.
IT'S HER SOFA.
IT'S HER HOUSE.

146
00:07:44.167 --> 00:07:46.767
 <i>IF YOU DON'T LIKE THE WAY</i>
 <i>THAT ROSEANNE KEEPS HOUSE.</i>

147
00:07:46.767 --> 00:07:49.534
THEN YOU TALK TO
ROSEANNE ABOUT IT.
YOU DON'T TALK TO ME.

148
00:07:49.534 --> 00:07:51.868
AND IF YOU DON'T LIKE
THE WAY THAT I RUN MY LIFE.

149
00:07:51.868 --> 00:07:54.367
THEN YOU TALK TO ME ABOUT IT.
YOU DON'T TALK TO ROSEANNE.

150
00:07:54.367 --> 00:07:57.901
WE'RE-- WE'RE SICK AND TIRED OF
THE WAY THAT YOU MANIPULATE US.

151
00:07:59.367 --> 00:08:01.300
IS THAT SO.
ROSEANNE?

152
00:08:05.434 --> 00:08:07.000
YEAH. RIGHT?

153
00:08:08.467 --> 00:08:12.601
WELL. MAYBE "MANIPULATE"
IS KIND OF A HARSH
WORD TO USE HERE.

154
00:08:12.601 --> 00:08:15.100
I JUST THINK
WHAT JACKIE MEANS.

155
00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:17.467
WHAT SHE'S TRYING TO
SAY IS THAT WE WISH
THAT YOU WOULD JUST

156
00:08:17.467 --> 00:08:20.734
TRY TO DEAL WITH US
IN A MORE DIRECT MANNER.

157
00:08:20.734 --> 00:08:22.234
YOU KNOW.
IF YOU WANT TO.

158
00:08:22.234 --> 00:08:24.667
NO. THAT'S NOT WHAT
JACKIE'S TRYING TO SAY.

159
00:08:24.667 --> 00:08:26.167
WHAT JACKIE'S
TRYING TO SAY--

160
00:08:26.167 --> 00:08:29.300
WHERE THE HELL WERE
YOU FIVE MINUTES AGO?

161
00:08:30.367 --> 00:08:33.267
I'LL GET SOME
SHEETS. MOM.

162
00:08:33.267 --> 00:08:36.234
YOU REALLY SHOULD TURN
YOUR MATTRESS MORE OFTEN.

163
00:08:38.133 --> 00:08:41.434
- WHERE ARE
 YOU GUYS GONNA SLEEP?
- ANYWHERE'S OKAY WITH ME.

164
00:08:41.434 --> 00:08:44.334
HEY. I DON'T
SLEEP ANYWHERE.

165
00:08:44.334 --> 00:08:46.868
WELL. THESE COTS
ARE PRETTY NICE.

166
00:08:46.868 --> 00:08:49.334
OH. I'M SURE MOM
AND DAD DON'T WANNA
SLEEP ON ANY COTS.

167
00:08:49.334 --> 00:08:50.834
WHAT DID WE DO
LAST TIME?

168
00:08:50.834 --> 00:08:52.334
LAST TIME?

169
00:08:53.667 --> 00:08:55.934
I'VE COMPLETELY BLOCKED IT
OUT OF MY MIND.

170
00:08:57.968 --> 00:09:00.501
YOU GUYS DON'T MIND
SLEEPING ON COTS. DO YOU?

171
00:09:00.501 --> 00:09:02.501
I CAN SLEEP
ANYWHERE.

172
00:09:02.501 --> 00:09:04.501
WHY DON'T YOU AND DAD
JUST TAKE ME AND DAN'S BED.

173
00:09:04.501 --> 00:09:06.033
AND WE'LL SLEEP
OUT HERE ON THE COTS?

174
00:09:06.033 --> 00:09:07.834
HONEY. I CAN'T SLEEP
ON THESE THINGS.

175
00:09:07.834 --> 00:09:10.100
LAST TIME DARLENE AND I
SLEPT DOWNSTAIRS ON THE COTS.

176
00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:12.133
AND GRANDMA AND GRANDPA
SLEPT UP IN OUR ROOM.

177
00:09:12.133 --> 00:09:14.133
I WANT TO SLEEP
ON THE SLEEPING BAGS.

178
00:09:14.133 --> 00:09:16.334
NO. THAT'S NOT WHAT
WE DID LAST YEAR.

179
00:09:16.334 --> 00:09:18.467
I'M VERY PARTICULAR
ABOUT WHERE I SLEEP.

180
00:09:18.467 --> 00:09:20.601
WHAT DOES THAT MEAN?

181
00:09:21.734 --> 00:09:24.601
I'LL TELL YOU
SOMETHING ABOUT ME.

182
00:09:24.601 --> 00:09:26.868
I'LL NEVER SLEEP
IN A COMMUNIST COUNTRY.

183
00:09:28.767 --> 00:09:30.767
I'LL VISIT ONE
DURING THE DAY.

184
00:09:30.767 --> 00:09:32.834
BUT I'LL NEVER SLEEP
IN ONE AT NIGHT.

185
00:09:32.834 --> 00:09:35.434
WELL. GOD BLESS
AMERICA.

186
00:09:35.434 --> 00:09:38.300
- CAN I SLEEP IN
 YOUR SLEEPING BAG?
- Roseanne: <i>NO. GO.</i>

187
00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:39.834
HOW ABOUT
WHAT I SAID?

188
00:09:39.834 --> 00:09:41.868
- WHAT DID YOU SAY?
- FORGET WHAT SHE SAID.

189
00:09:41.868 --> 00:09:43.868
PLEASE. LET'S NOT
FUSS ABOUT THIS.

190
00:09:43.868 --> 00:09:46.133
DAD AND I CAN
SLEEP ANYWHERE.

191
00:09:46.133 --> 00:09:49.534
DARLENE AND I SLEPT
ON THE COTS. AND GRANDMA
AND GRANDPA HAD OUR ROOM.

192
00:09:49.534 --> 00:09:53.000
THESE COTS STILL SMELL
FROM WHEN WE FOUND
THE DEAD PIGEON IN IT.

193
00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.000
- DARLENE.
- Jackie: <i>OKAY.</i>

194
00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:58.634
D.J. AND I MUST HAVE
BOTH SLEPT ON THE FLOOR.
MOM AND DAD HAD D.J.'S BED--

195
00:09:58.634 --> 00:10:00.567
BUT THAT COULDN'T HAVE BEEN.
BECAUSE D.J.'S BED'S TOO SMALL

196
00:10:00.567 --> 00:10:02.100
AND THEY WOULD HAVE
BEEN UNCOMFORTABLE.

197
00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:04.634
JACKIE. YOU WERE
NOT EVEN HERE.

198
00:10:04.634 --> 00:10:05.968
TEMPER. TEMPER.

199
00:10:05.968 --> 00:10:08.067
THEN HOW COME
I CAN REMEMBER IT?

200
00:10:08.067 --> 00:10:10.901
BECAUSE YOU HAVE
TOTAL RECALL OF ALL
THINGS IMAGINARY!

201
00:10:10.901 --> 00:10:13.400
GIRLS. GIRLS.

202
00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:15.234
LET'S BE LADIES.
SHALL WE?

203
00:10:15.234 --> 00:10:17.234
CAN WE COME TO SOME
SORT OF CONCLUSION HERE?

204
00:10:17.234 --> 00:10:19.467
OKAY. YOU WANT A CONCLUSION?
I'LL GIVE YOU A CONCLUSION.

205
00:10:19.467 --> 00:10:22.067
OKAY. JACKIE. YOU GO
SLEEP IN D.J.'S BED.

206
00:10:22.067 --> 00:10:24.067
 <i>D.J.. SLEEP IN</i>
 <i>A SLEEPING BAG!</i>

207
00:10:24.067 --> 00:10:27.300
GIRLS. GIRLS. GIRLS.
LET'S JUST BE LITTLE LADIES

208
00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:29.767
AND GO UP AND SLEEP
IN YOUR OWN BED.

209
00:10:29.767 --> 00:10:32.434
- MOM AND DAD. YOU TAKE
 ME AND DAN'S ROOM.
- WAIT A MINUTE.

210
00:10:32.434 --> 00:10:35.634
AND I'M GONNA
SLEEP HERE ON THE COT.
AND SO IS MR. FLEXIBLE.

211
00:10:36.834 --> 00:10:39.501
HOPEFULLY WE WON'T
HAVE ALL THIS CONFUSION

212
00:10:39.501 --> 00:10:42.000
ONCE YOUR FATHER AND I
HAVE OUR OWN PLACE

213
00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.167
RIGHT HERE
IN LANFORD.

214
00:10:44.167 --> 00:10:46.367
SLEEP TIGHT.
EVERYONE.

215
00:10:47.601 --> 00:10:49.033
NIGHTY NIGHT.

216
00:10:53.501 --> 00:10:55.634
DAN. ARE YOU
SLEEPING?

217
00:10:56.901 --> 00:10:58.501
LIKE A BABY.

218
00:11:00.634 --> 00:11:04.934
THE FACT THAT IT'S 4:30
IN THE MORNING AND I HAVE
A SPRING IN MY PANCREAS

219
00:11:04.934 --> 00:11:08.067
ISN'T KEEPING ME AWAKE
THE LEAST LITTLE BIT.

220
00:11:08.067 --> 00:11:10.067
IF MY PARENTS
MOVE TO LANFORD.

221
00:11:10.067 --> 00:11:13.033
I AM GONNA BE SLEEPING
ON A COT FOR THE REST
OF MY LIFE.

222
00:11:13.033 --> 00:11:16.133
BECAUSE I'M GONNA
BE IN PRISON FOR
BLOWING 'EM AWAY.

223
00:11:17.501 --> 00:11:20.033
HONEY. HONEY.
BE REALISTIC.

224
00:11:20.033 --> 00:11:22.567
YOU DON'T KNOW
HOW TO USE A GUN.

225
00:11:22.567 --> 00:11:24.868
I'LL DO IT.

226
00:11:26.801 --> 00:11:30.000
SERIOUSLY. DAN.
WHAT ARE WE GONNA DO?

227
00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.534
WELL. I'D SAY
"LET'S SLEEP ON IT."

228
00:11:32.534 --> 00:11:34.467
BUT WHO CAN SLEEP?!

229
00:11:35.901 --> 00:11:38.234
YOU KNOW. IF YOU KNEW HOW
TO STAND UP TO YOUR PARENTS.

230
00:11:38.234 --> 00:11:40.234
WE WOULDN'T BE
LYING HERE RIGHT NOW.

231
00:11:40.234 --> 00:11:41.901
 <i>WHAT IS THAT</i>
 <i>SUPPOSED TO MEAN?</i>

232
00:11:41.901 --> 00:11:44.901
AND I'M WARNING YOU. THAT
FIREPLACE POKER'S WITHIN REACH.

233
00:11:44.901 --> 00:11:48.334
BABY. LET'S NOT
GET INTO THIS RIGHT NOW.

234
00:11:48.334 --> 00:11:52.767
BECAUSE IT'S NOT MY WARPED.
PSYCHOTIC. NEUROTIC PARENTS
THAT ARE LAYING IN MY BED.

235
00:11:55.767 --> 00:11:59.033
- I'M GONNA GO SIT ON THE PORCH.
- Dan: <i>HONEY. HONEY.</i>

236
00:11:59.033 --> 00:12:01.033
HONEY. LET'S NOT
DO THIS TO EACH OTHER.

237
00:12:01.033 --> 00:12:03.400
COME ON. BABY.
I'M SORRY.

238
00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:05.968
I'M JUST ANGRY
'CAUSE I HAVEN'T SLEPT.

239
00:12:05.968 --> 00:12:08.467
WE GOT A COUPLE HOURS
LEFT TILL DAYLIGHT.

240
00:12:08.467 --> 00:12:11.067
LET'S JUST TRY
TO SALVAGE SOME SLEEP.

241
00:12:28.634 --> 00:12:31.167
 <i>( crickets chirping )</i>

242
00:12:37.801 --> 00:12:40.067
( Al clears throat )

243
00:12:44.434 --> 00:12:46.033
Mom: <i>AL?</i>

244
00:12:47.567 --> 00:12:49.100
- AL?
- RIGHT HERE.

245
00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:51.467
OH. YOU TWO
GO BACK TO SLEEP.

246
00:12:51.467 --> 00:12:54.567
I'M JUST GONNA MAKE
YOUR FATHER BREAKFAST.
HE ALWAYS GETS UP AT 4:30.

247
00:12:54.567 --> 00:12:57.167
WHY? I DON'T KNOW.
GO BACK TO SLEEP.

248
00:12:58.234 --> 00:13:00.801
FEEL LIKE MAKING LOVE?

249
00:13:09.767 --> 00:13:11.267
DON'T GET UP.

250
00:13:11.267 --> 00:13:14.267
I JUST WANT TO
KNOW WHERE YOU KEEP
YOUR CITRUS FRUIT.

251
00:13:14.267 --> 00:13:17.968
I THINK THERE'S SOME STRAWBERRY
POP-TARTS IN THE FRIDGE.

252
00:13:17.968 --> 00:13:21.701
YOUR FATHER NEEDS TO HAVE
A PIECE OF CITRUS FRUIT.

253
00:13:21.701 --> 00:13:24.300
I THINK THERE'S AN ORANGE
UNDER THE DRYER.

254
00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:26.300
GO BACK TO SLEEP.

255
00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:29.300
DAN SHOULDN'T SLEEP
ON HIS LEFT SIDE.
IT'S BAD FOR THE HEART.

256
00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:31.234
SO'S A RUSTY SPIKE.

257
00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:37.667
THIS IS NUTS.
THIS IS NUTS.

258
00:13:37.667 --> 00:13:39.968
I GOT A NEW JOB
TO START TODAY.

259
00:13:39.968 --> 00:13:41.801
I'VE GOTTA GO TO
WORK TOO. YOU KNOW.

260
00:13:41.801 --> 00:13:45.334
WELL. WHY DON'T YOU
GO IN THERE AND TELL
MA AND PA KETTLE TO SHUT UP?

261
00:13:46.434 --> 00:13:49.033
WHAT ARE YOU DOING UP
SO EARLY?

262
00:13:57.701 --> 00:13:59.901
YOU KNOW. THIS IS
THE BEST ROOM IN YOUR HOUSE.

263
00:13:59.901 --> 00:14:02.934
YEAH. 'CAUSE MOM
AND DAD AREN'T IN IT.

264
00:14:02.934 --> 00:14:05.200
THIS IS OUR ONLY
SANCTUARY FROM THEM.

265
00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:06.734
WELL. DON'T
COUNT ON IT.

266
00:14:06.734 --> 00:14:09.300
SHE'LL FIGURE OUT
SOME WAY TO GET IN HERE.

267
00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:13.200
AND THEN YOU CAN
STAND UP TO HERE AGAIN
LIKE YOU DID BEFORE.

268
00:14:14.734 --> 00:14:16.767
I SAID
TO YOUR GRANDMOTHER.

269
00:14:16.767 --> 00:14:18.234
"BEVERLY"--

270
00:14:18.234 --> 00:14:20.567
I CALL HER BEVERLY
BECAUSE THAT'S HER NAME.

271
00:14:21.634 --> 00:14:23.367
I SAID. "BEVERLY.

272
00:14:23.367 --> 00:14:26.968
THIS YEAR I'M GONNA
PAY MORE ATTENTION TO
MY STABLE AND HORSES."

273
00:14:26.968 --> 00:14:28.968
YOU DON'T HAVE
ANY HORSES. GRANDPA.

274
00:14:28.968 --> 00:14:30.968
'CAUSE I DON'T
HAVE A STABLE.

275
00:14:30.968 --> 00:14:33.067
- PULL MY FINGER. KID.
- DON'T.

276
00:14:35.567 --> 00:14:37.567
I'M SORRY.
WHAT WERE YOU SAYING?

277
00:14:37.567 --> 00:14:39.767
OH. I'M FINISHED.

278
00:14:40.834 --> 00:14:42.834
ARE YOU GUYS GETTING
READY FOR SCHOOL?

279
00:14:42.834 --> 00:14:44.534
YEAH. AND WE'RE REALLY
EXCITED ABOUT IT.

280
00:14:44.534 --> 00:14:46.000
THAT'S GREAT.

281
00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:49.200
THEY'RE REALLY DOING
GREAT IN SCHOOL.

282
00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:52.534
AL WAS ALWAYS VERY CONCERNED
WITH THE CHILDREN'S EDUCATION.

283
00:14:52.534 --> 00:14:54.734
HE WAS SOME FATHER.

284
00:14:54.734 --> 00:14:56.901
WHAT IS IT YOU
ALWAYS USED TO SAY?

285
00:14:56.901 --> 00:15:00.167
YOU CAN LEAD
A HORSE TO WATER.

286
00:15:00.167 --> 00:15:02.501
BUT YOU CAN'T
MAKE 'EM THINK.

287
00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:07.234
YOU USED TO SAY THAT?

288
00:15:08.534 --> 00:15:10.467
AND YOU STOPPED
SAYING THAT?

289
00:15:13.567 --> 00:15:15.834
HE USED TO SAY THAT.

290
00:15:15.834 --> 00:15:18.367
AND HE DOESN'T
SAY IT ANYMORE.

291
00:15:18.367 --> 00:15:20.234
HE USED TO SAY.

292
00:15:20.234 --> 00:15:22.667
"YOU CAN LEAD
A HORSE TO WATER.

293
00:15:22.667 --> 00:15:25.234
BUT YOU CAN'T
MAKE 'EM THINK."

294
00:15:25.234 --> 00:15:27.434
AND HE DOESN'T
SAY IT ANYMORE.

295
00:15:28.901 --> 00:15:30.801
I HAVEN'T SLEPT.

296
00:15:36.567 --> 00:15:38.667
I SWEAR WE'RE
ONLY SANE TODAY

297
00:15:38.667 --> 00:15:40.667
BECAUSE WE KEPT
EACH OTHER THAT WAY.

298
00:15:40.667 --> 00:15:44.601
I KNOW. WE PROTECTED
EACH OTHER FROM MR.
AND MRS. TOTAL INSANITY.

299
00:15:44.601 --> 00:15:47.200
YEAH. LIKE THAT TIME THAT
YOU WERE IN THE EIGHTH GRADE

300
00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:50.367
AND YOU WERE DATING
THAT 40-YEAR-OLD GUY.

301
00:15:50.367 --> 00:15:52.601
- <i>AAH!</i>
- HE WAS NOT 40.

302
00:15:52.601 --> 00:15:54.934
OH. HE WAS THE ONLY GUY
AT YOUR FRESHMAN DANCE

303
00:15:54.934 --> 00:15:58.267
THAT WAS
WEARING A TOUPEE.

304
00:15:58.267 --> 00:16:00.501
I TOLD MOM
HE WAS YOUR TUTOR.

305
00:16:00.501 --> 00:16:03.100
AND I TAUGHT HIM
MORE THAN HE TAUGHT ME.

306
00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:05.167
WELL. THAT'S
THE WAY IT GOES.

307
00:16:05.167 --> 00:16:07.801
THE BOTTOM LINE
IS THAT

308
00:16:07.801 --> 00:16:11.267
MOM AND DAD ARE
JUST SO OUT THERE.

309
00:16:11.267 --> 00:16:14.567
WELL. YOU KNOW.
IT'S NOT ALL THEIR FAULT.

310
00:16:14.567 --> 00:16:16.801
WE SHOULD SHOW 'EM
A LITTLE COMPASSION.

311
00:16:16.801 --> 00:16:18.801
WELL. HERE
WE GO AGAIN.

312
00:16:18.801 --> 00:16:21.634
CHECKING YOUR BACKBONE
AT THE DOOR.

313
00:16:21.634 --> 00:16:24.100
WELL. FINE.
YOU BLAME YOUR
WHOLE LIFE--

314
00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:26.467
OH. ROSEANNE.
YOU TURN INTO
A LITTLE ROBOT

315
00:16:26.467 --> 00:16:28.467
EVERY TIME MOM
AND DAD COME AROUND.

316
00:16:28.467 --> 00:16:32.067
YOU TURN INTO LITTLE ROSIE
TWO-SHOES. AND I'M SICK OF IT.

317
00:16:32.067 --> 00:16:36.167
HEY. PEOPLE WHO LIVE IN
COCKROACH-INFESTED APARTMENTS
SHOULD NOT THROW STONES.

318
00:16:36.167 --> 00:16:37.934
- I CAN'T EVEN TALK TO YOU!
- OH. SHUT UP!

319
00:16:37.934 --> 00:16:39.601
YOU ALWAYS HAVE
TO GET YOUR OWN WAY.

320
00:16:39.601 --> 00:16:42.033
IT HAS TO BE MY WAY
WHEN YOU'RE STANDING
HERE IN MY BATHROOM

321
00:16:42.033 --> 00:16:43.634
AT 7:30 IN THE MORNING

322
00:16:43.634 --> 00:16:46.701
AFTER MY PARENTS CAME OVER
TO MY HOUSE AND DECIMATE
MY WHOLE FAMILY.

323
00:16:46.701 --> 00:16:48.200
NOW THEY'RE YOUR
PARENTS. FINE.

324
00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:50.701
IF YOU WANT 'EM.
FINE. YOU HAVE 'EM!

325
00:16:50.701 --> 00:16:52.834
GEE. YOU TELL ME WHEN
IT'S THEIR ANNIVERSARY.

326
00:16:52.834 --> 00:16:55.868
- AND YOU LET 'EM STAY AT YOUR
 HOUSE NEXT TIME THEY COME...
- FINE. GOOD.

327
00:16:55.868 --> 00:16:58.567
AND DECIMATE YOUR WHOLE FAMILY.
OF WHICH YOU DON'T EVEN HAVE.

328
00:16:58.567 --> 00:17:02.534
BECAUSE YOU CAN'T CONCENTRATE
ON NOTHING LONG ENOUGH THAN
IT TAKES TO CHUG A BEER!

329
00:17:04.467 --> 00:17:07.000
AND DON'T GIVE ME THAT WOUNDED
LITTLE JACKIE LOOK EITHER.

330
00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:10.033
BECAUSE THAT ONLY WORKS ON GUYS
NAMED MIKE WHO DRIVE EL CAMINOS.

331
00:17:11.701 --> 00:17:14.267
VERY DRAMATIC.
ROSEANNE.

332
00:17:14.267 --> 00:17:17.834
OH. SO NOW YOU'RE
NOT GONNA TALK TO ME.

333
00:17:17.834 --> 00:17:21.334
GOD. WOULD I LOVE TO
THROW A HAMMER THROUGH
A PLATE GLASS WINDOW.

334
00:17:22.667 --> 00:17:24.667
DON'T WAIT FOR
A RESPONSE. DAN.

335
00:17:24.667 --> 00:17:27.067
HER MAJESTY'S
NOT SPEAKING TO
ANYBODY TODAY.

336
00:17:27.067 --> 00:17:30.767
- JACKIE. WHO EVEN ASKED YOU?
- HEY. I'M A PART OF
 THIS FAMILY TOO.

337
00:17:30.767 --> 00:17:33.200
YEAH. WHEN YOUR HAMPER'S FULL
OR YOUR CAR NEEDS WORKING ON.

338
00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:36.400
I'VE BEEN A MEMBER OF THIS
FAMILY LONGER THAN YOU HAVE!

339
00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:39.367
( laughing )
BOY. THAT'S SOMETHING
TO BE PROUD OF!

340
00:17:41.701 --> 00:17:44.033
YOU KNOW. I SAW A WHOLE THING
ABOUT THIS ON <i>OPRAH.</i>

341
00:17:44.033 --> 00:17:45.534
AND THAT'S
JUST WHAT WE ARE TOO.

342
00:17:45.534 --> 00:17:49.467
WE'RE JUST LIKE THAT.
WE ARE A DYSFUNCTIONAL FAMILY!

343
00:17:51.367 --> 00:17:53.334
( screams )

344
00:17:57.167 --> 00:17:59.834
THANKS. GRAMPS.
BYE. GRAM.

345
00:17:59.834 --> 00:18:03.234
- Al: BYE. BECKY.
- Beverly: BYE. DEAR.

346
00:18:03.234 --> 00:18:06.000
GRANDPA SAID HE'D BUY ME
A HORSE NEXT YEAR.

347
00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:09.334
YEAH. WELL. GRANDPA'S
SADDLE'S ON TOO TIGHT.

348
00:18:09.334 --> 00:18:10.934
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

349
00:18:10.934 --> 00:18:13.234
I'M MAKING BREAKFAST
FOR MY KIDS.

350
00:18:13.234 --> 00:18:15.501
I ALREADY MADE
THEM BREAKFAST.

351
00:18:15.501 --> 00:18:17.567
GO TO SCHOOL THEN.

352
00:18:17.567 --> 00:18:20.000
- BYE.
- Al: BYE. KIDS.

353
00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:23.300
YEAH. SHE MADE 'EM BREAKFAST.
CEREAL AND CHOCOLATE
CHIP COOKIES.

354
00:18:23.300 --> 00:18:25.367
YOUR FATHER GAVE
THEM THE COOKIES.

355
00:18:25.367 --> 00:18:29.100
WHETHER THEY EAT 'EM
NOW OR IN THE AFTERNOON.
WHAT'S THE DIFFERENCE?

356
00:18:30.167 --> 00:18:31.834
YOU WANT TO KNOW
THE DIFFERENCE?

357
00:18:31.834 --> 00:18:33.834
I'LL TELL YOU WHAT
THE DIFFERENCE IS.

358
00:18:33.834 --> 00:18:38.033
THE DIFFERENCE IS.
YOU SHOW UP AT MY DOOR
UNANNOUNCED. UNINVITED.

359
00:18:38.033 --> 00:18:40.400
YOU JUST DRIVE EVERYBODY
AND WORK 'EM UP INTO A FRENZY

360
00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:42.067
UNTIL WE'RE READY
TO KILL EACH OTHER!

361
00:18:42.067 --> 00:18:45.434
WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT?
WE'RE HAVING A NICE BREAKFAST.

362
00:18:45.434 --> 00:18:48.000
I'M TALKING ABOUT.
IF YOU GUYS ARE GONNA
MOVE HERE TO LANFORD.

363
00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:50.467
YOU HAVE GOT TO MOVE
ONTO THE WHOLE OTHER
SIDE OF THIS TOWN.

364
00:18:50.467 --> 00:18:53.033
BECAUSE I AM NOT GONNA
BE ABLE TO TAKE THIS
FOR THE REST OF MY LIFE.

365
00:18:53.033 --> 00:18:55.167
WHO'S MOVING
TO LANFORD?

366
00:18:55.167 --> 00:18:58.167
YOU GUYS ARE.
YOU SAID SO LAST NIGHT.

367
00:18:58.167 --> 00:19:01.501
OH. WE'RE NEVER GONNA
MOVE INTO LANFORD.

368
00:19:01.501 --> 00:19:04.000
WE WERE JUST THINKING.
WE WERE JUST TALKING.

369
00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:07.100
WHY DO YOU TAKE
EVERYTHING SO SERIOUSLY?

370
00:19:07.100 --> 00:19:09.701
SO YOU'RE
NOT MOVING?

371
00:19:09.701 --> 00:19:11.767
NO. IN FACT.
WE'VE GOT TO GET GOING.

372
00:19:11.767 --> 00:19:14.400
WE'RE ON OUR WAY TO
SEE COUSIN SYDNEY
IN BEAUFORD.

373
00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:16.400
HE HAD GUM SURGERY.

374
00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:18.334
I'M GONNA BUY HIM
SOME ROCK CANDY.

375
00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:24.701
WELL. IT'S A SHAME
YOU COULDN'T STAY LONGER.

376
00:19:26.167 --> 00:19:28.834
DAN. DO YOU REALLY
MEAN THAT?

377
00:19:28.834 --> 00:19:32.400
HEY. IF YOU DON'T THINK
YOU GUYS LEAVING IS
GONNA AFFECT EVERYBODY.

378
00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:34.100
YOU'RE CRAZY.

379
00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:36.300
AL. DID YOU HEAR THAT?

380
00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:38.434
YEAH. I'D GIVE HIM
A BIG KISS...

381
00:19:38.434 --> 00:19:41.234
- OH.
- ...IF I LIKED BOYS.

382
00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:50.100
OH. MOM. I'M REALLY
GONNA MISS YOU.

383
00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:51.634
ME TOO.

384
00:19:55.467 --> 00:19:57.033
BIG HUG.

385
00:19:57.033 --> 00:19:59.434
THIS HAS BEEN
A GREAT VISIT.

386
00:19:59.434 --> 00:20:03.033
OH. THIS HAS BEEN
A WONDERFUL VISIT.

387
00:20:03.033 --> 00:20:05.300
Al:
 <i>LET ME DO IT AGAIN.</i>

388
00:20:11.567 --> 00:20:15.167
AND THE SICK THING IS
THAT I KIND OF MISS 'EM.

389
00:20:15.167 --> 00:20:16.767
I KIND OF DON'T.

390
00:20:20.334 --> 00:20:21.834
DAN?

391
00:20:21.834 --> 00:20:23.567
WHAT-EE?

392
00:20:23.567 --> 00:20:25.267
PULL MY FINGER.

393
00:20:34.834 --> 00:20:37.167
AAH!

394
00:20:37.167 --> 00:20:39.100
AAH!

395
00:20:52.901 --> 00:20:54.734
Dan: <i>HERE'S THE DEAL.</i>

396
00:20:54.734 --> 00:20:57.400
I'LL GET THE CHECKBOOK OUT.
BUT I GOTTA WATCH.

397
00:21:00.234 --> 00:21:02.868
- HEY. WHAT A SURPRISE.
- I WAS GUNNA DO THE LINE.

398
00:21:02.868 --> 00:21:06.334
WELL. I'M NOT WORKING.
SO I THOUGHT I'D COME
OVER AND GET SOME LINES.

399
00:21:06.334 --> 00:21:07.834
I'M GONNA GET
OUT OF HERE.

400
00:21:07.834 --> 00:21:09.767
HOW NICE.
THAT WAS FUN.
